    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Chrysanthemum and Stream by Ogata Korin (1658~ 1716)\nm and Stream by\nOne of Japan's enduring art forms, the decorated fan is a beautiful and\nnouring al\nuseful device widely popular even today. It has a wide range of uses.\nIsetul device widely popu\nserving as an integral part of many classical dances.\nand a diverse\nnumber of other uses.\nincluding, of course, that of cooling the brow.\nThe design for this fan is a stylized stream and chrysanthemums.\nJapan's national flower. Executed on a gold ground, the red and yellow\nchrysanthemums have been applied with an impasto technique in combi-\nlated\nnation with leaves painted in an abbreviated style. These elements.\ntogether with the stylized stream, produce a splendid effect. The artist.\nKorin, was one of Japan's greatest decorative painters.\nJAL hopes this hand-made fan will serve as a remembrance of our\nservice to you\nJAPAN AIR LINES\n(1658~1716)",
      "JAPAN AIR LINES"
    ],
